From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: sunxi: sun55i-pck600: read the boot state, do not assert it

keep_boot_state registers every A733 domain GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON and passes
is_off = false to pm_genpd_init(), i.e. it tells genpd that every domain is
powered because the boot firmware left it that way. On this SoC that is true
for ten of eleven domains and false for the eleventh, and the failure mode of
being wrong is the worst kind.

Measured on the 8 GiB board, 2026-09-07, our own image with nothing bound to the GPU:
GPU_CORE (index 6) reads PWPR = 0x8 and PWSR = 0x0 -- requested on, reported
off -- while the other ten read 0x8 in both. The same window reads 0x8 on the
vendor kernel with its DDK loaded, so the domain is real and it does come up;
what does not happen is the handshake, on our boot.

What that costs today, also measured on the 8 GiB board the same day, one variable at a
time, with the markers on the UART because an ssh pipe buffers and returns
nothing when the board dies:

  block unclocked, read 0x01800000 (core, in GPU_CORE)   -> 0x0, board lives
  block clocked,   read 0x01880000 (wrapper, in GPU_TOP) -> 0x0, board lives
  block clocked,   read 0x01800000 (core, in GPU_CORE)   -> SoC stops, silent

The console ends mid-trace with no panic and no line on any CPU. That is the
same stop the powervr bind produces, and the provider is what makes it silent:
it declares the domain powered, the consumer binds on that word, and the first
access into an unsupplied block never returns.

So read PWSR instead. A domain that reads on keeps exactly today's behaviour --
ALWAYS_ON, is_off = false -- which is what USB2/dwc3, the current consumer,
depends on and what every other boot-on domain gets. A domain that reads off is
registered off and named in a dev_warn, so the first consumer that needs it goes
through power_on(), and that path already exists upstream: it writes PWPR and
polls PWSR with a 10 ms timeout, then fails with a message. An attach that
cannot be supplied now fails the probe instead of stopping the SoC.

ALWAYS_ON is set only on the domains that really are on, and the first cut of
this patch got that wrong. It kept the flag on both branches, reasoning that
genpd must never gate a domain on this SoC. genpd refused: pm_genpd_init()
returns -EINVAL for a domain flagged always-on and handed an off state, the
provider failed to register at all, and 6a00000.usb went to deferred probe with
"supplier 7060000.power-controller not ready". Seen on the 8 GiB board, boot of
2026-09-07. The rejection is correct -- nothing may be promised to stay up that
is not up -- so a domain reading off is left gateable. That costs nothing here:
it is already off, and this SoC ignores a PWPR write on it in either direction,
which was measured the same day on the vendor stack with the DDK unloaded.

The A523 path (keep_boot_state = false) is untouched.

Falsifiers:
 - ✅ on our image the probe prints the dev_warn for GPU_CORE and for no other
   domain -- observed on a test build, boot of 2026-09-07, verbatim:
   'domain "GPU_CORE" is not powered at boot (PWSR reads off)';
 - ✅ USB2/dwc3 still attaches and enumerates exactly as before -- FAILED on the
   first cut for the reason above; met by the fix on the 8 GiB board,
   2026-09-07: pm_genpd_summary shows "USB2 on" with "6a00000.usb active ... SW"
   under it, six roothubs and fourteen device entries;
 - ⬜ with the GPU node enabled, powervr's attach fails with the PWSR timeout
   message and the board survives it -- not testable from this branch, which
   carries no powervr module; it needs this patch on a tree that also carries the powervr GPU driver.

Falsifiers 1 and 2 are met on hardware; 3 stays open until this patch runs together with the powervr GPU driver.

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
@@ -117,6 +117,22 @@
 	return sunxi_pck600_pd_set_power(pd, false);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Read a domain's actual power state out of PWSR.
+ *
+ * PWPR carries the requested policy and PWSR the status the PPU reports back;
+ * the two disagree on a domain whose handshake does not complete. Registering
+ * such a domain as powered is what turns a failed power-up into a silent stop
+ * later, when a consumer touches the block, so the boot state is read here and
+ * never assumed.
+ */
+static bool sunxi_pck600_pd_is_on(struct sunxi_pck600_pd *pd)
+{
+	u32 reg = readl(pd->base + PPU_PWSR);
+
+	return FIELD_GET(PPU_PWR_STATUS, reg) == PPU_POWER_MODE_ON;
+}
+
 static void sunxi_pck600_pd_setup(struct sunxi_pck600_pd *pd,
 				  const struct sunxi_pck600_desc *desc)
 {
@@ -176,19 +192,48 @@
 
 	for (i = 0; i < desc->num_domains; i++) {
 		struct sunxi_pck600_pd *pd = &pck->pds[i];
+		bool is_off;
 
 		pd->genpd.name = desc->pd_names[i];
 		pd->genpd.power_off = sunxi_pck600_power_off;
 		pd->genpd.power_on = sunxi_pck600_power_on;
 		pd->base = base + PPU_REG_SIZE * i;
 
-		if (desc->keep_boot_state)
-			pd->genpd.flags = GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON;
-		else
+		if (desc->keep_boot_state) {
+			/*
+			 * Hold the boot state -- but the state that is there,
+			 * not the one that is convenient. A domain reading off
+			 * is registered off, so the first consumer to need it
+			 * goes through power_on(), which writes PWPR and polls
+			 * PWSR with a timeout and fails the attach with a
+			 * message. Without this the provider declares such a
+			 * domain powered, the consumer binds, and the first
+			 * access into an unsupplied block stops the SoC with
+			 * nothing on the console.
+			 *
+			 * ALWAYS_ON is set only on the domains that really are
+			 * on. genpd rejects the pair outright --
+			 * pm_genpd_init() returns -EINVAL for a domain that is
+			 * flagged always-on and handed an off state -- and it
+			 * is right to: nothing may be promised to stay up that
+			 * is not up. A domain reading off is therefore left
+			 * gateable, which costs nothing, because it is already
+			 * off and this SoC ignores a PWPR write on it either
+			 * way.
+			 */
+			is_off = !sunxi_pck600_pd_is_on(pd);
+			if (is_off)
+				dev_warn(dev,
+					 "domain \"%s\" is not powered at boot (PWSR reads off)\n",
+					 pd->genpd.name);
+			else
+				pd->genpd.flags = GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON;
+		} else {
 			sunxi_pck600_pd_setup(pd, desc);
+			is_off = false;
+		}
 
-		/* "false" => domain starts powered (its boot state). */
-		ret = pm_genpd_init(&pd->genpd, NULL, false);
+		ret = pm_genpd_init(&pd->genpd, NULL, is_off);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "failed to initialize power domain\n");
 			goto err_remove_pds;
